    "m_Title": "Reciprocal",
    "m_Content": "Reciprocal flips the control so higher values = tighter surface detail, even though UV math works backwards.\n\nBigger UV numbers → texture stretches → LESS detail\n\nSmaller UV numbers → texture shrinks → MORE detail\n\nreciprocal(x) = 1 / x\n\nUV × (1 / Scale)\r\n\n\nNormals \t  Reciprocal\t\tUV multiplier\tResult\n     1\t\t    1 / 1 = 1\t\t     ×1\t\t\tnormal\n     2\t\t    1 / 2 = .5\t\t    ×0.5\t\ttighter\n     4\t\t    1 / 4 = .25\t   ×0.25\t         very tight\n",
